how to balance your life and your work  i got a great question from one of my  youtube viewers love you guys  zonato25 who wrote in to say i'm a 16  year old entrepreneur and one of my  biggest misunderstood concepts  is about living your life sometimes i  want to party celebrate have fun or even  travel listen some loud music  but at the same time i wish to improve  in my personal skills study and work  more one day to be remembered by some  great contribution i've done to  humankind my question is  how can i have fun and live life at the  same time  i'm working or studying so this is a  great question i love this question  and i'm going to do my best to answer  this in a video i have a whole series of  zuga guides on time management that i  think will really help break this down  i'm gonna try to do this in a short  video for you  so i have three ideas for you okay three  rules to follow  the first one is follow your passion  number one is follow your passion and  you need to be doing things in your life  or in your business  or at school that that you're passionate  about that you love doing  when you are not doing something that  you're passionate about life sucks  okay and this is an interesting case  because  that passion may change in your business  you might get really excited about  something  and that lasts for a certain amount of  time but then that may switch  you know i i've been involved in a  number of projects that i was really  excited about at the start  and then the passion dove i wasn't  interested anymore  and that's when you don't just force  yourself to keep going on it you swerve  and find a different direction  there's some projects that i've loved  doing that i still love doing like these  videos  i still love doing these videos i love  helping you guys out and so i keep doing  it you know wednesdays when i sit down  and do these videos  it's one of the best days of my week i  look forward to it every week  if it ever gets to the point where i'm  like oh man wednesdays  oh socks i gotta go do more videos  if i get to that point i will not have a  lot of success  forcing myself to keep doing videos when  i'm not excited by it  i'll have to stop doing videos swerve  and do something else  and hopefully the day doesn't count but  you never know  so you have to follow your passion okay  and that applies to your life too if  you're if you're  you know looking at dancing or listening  to music or going to parties or whatever  has  something you're passionate about number  two create a schedule  this may not work for everybody but i  like having a structure  i like knowing that i can plan things  out for the week and that everything  will fit  so you know you think about what your  week looks like  monday to friday and then weekends and  think about all the different things  that you want to get done during that  week and schedule them in  put them in your calendars hey this is  what i'm going to spend time on studying  i'm going to spend time on my business  i'm going to spend time with my friends  and fun  and the friends and fun part is just as  important right if you're just all  business  all the time you're going to burn out  and you're not going to like your  business anymore right so it has to be  that mix whatever you feel is right for  you and schedule it in  for me i like knowing it's it's one  having the confidence  and knowing that i have time scheduled  out so  sometimes you can feel overwhelmed right  you have so many things on the go so  many things you have to do so many  people to get back to like when am i  going to do all this stuff i'm going to  go crazy  so i find that having the schedule helps  me because i know okay i don't have to  write back to him today  i don't have to get that proposal done  today but i have time on thursday  to do it i have time that's we're going  to do everything so having that  just gives me more confidence and  reduces my stress level  and uh when you're an entrepreneur it's  good to find things that reduce your  stress level  and so block everything out your  personal and your business  the last one is go with the flow  and this one is breaking rule number two  you will find that there will be times  where you were in a state of flow  where it does not make sense to keep on  your schedule it's worth  breaking your schedule because you're in  a state of flow  and what i mean by that is there will be  times when if you look on a business  perspective there'll be times when  you're just really in the in the groove  like you are  if you're writing something you're  feeling it you're making so much  progress if you're doing videos you're  like you're just you're feeling it right  you're really into it you're doing a  great job  you're all excited you have to stay  there  you have to push everything else off  that day and stay there for as long as  you can there'll be times when  you know you you start doing something  at nine in the morning you wake up or  you look up and it's five at night  and you're still working on it like what  just happened to the day  i remember my first moments of that were  playing games like command and conquer  or civilization you could burn like  eight hours and you don't know where the  day went  but i get that in my business too and  when i'm in that  zone i try to stay there because getting  there is so hard you don't get that  every day  and the stuff you're going to create  when you're in that zone is going to be  so much better than any other time  so you have to cancel i've pushed  meetings i've pushed other appointments  i've pushed other projects because i'm  in the flow on something and i really  enjoy doing it and i know what i'm  creating is going to be  amazing so don't fool yourself to say ah  you know what this schoolwork i'm in the  flow i'm doing so well  i'm going to keep going on it that's bs  you know you don't trick yourself  but when you're really in that zone and  you know when you're in it you've been  there before  you don't get that every day when you're  in that zone you have to keep going  and that can also apply to your personal  life so there's been days where  i'm working on my business and i'm on my  schedule and  uh you know it's just i'm not feeling it  for some  some reason today just i'm not i can't  get in it i i'm struggling with  everything i'm doing  and i look outside and it's a beautiful  day and i just feel like going for a  walk  you know like enjoy the day outside  because because i am not getting  progress on my business  the right answer at least for me is not  push through  grind it out create crappy work that i'm  just gonna have to fix the next day  and then resent my business because i  missed out on a great day  i might go out and enjoy the day and  i'll feel better  and i'll feel happy that i'm an  entrepreneur and i can set my own time  and the next day i come back and i get  to work i'll be in a much better mood  much better space and able to create  something amazing  again so you have to follow the flow you  have to follow your momentum but stick  within a schedule when you're not on  your flow if that makes sense  okay so number one follow your passion  number two create a schedule that works  for you and it's okay if that schedule  changes so if you feel like you're  you're doing something that's working  for a couple months and then it doesn't  feel right anymore  change the schedule up i change my  schedule a lot  every couple months i'm changing my  schedule around a little bit and then  three go with the flow  and when you're really feeling something  something amazing is happening right now  you have to stay in that zone  and not let anything keep you distracted  i hope that helps those are my tips you  guys liked the video please give it a  thumbs up below  let me know what you think leave a  comment underneath if you have a  question for me  leave it below i'll make a video  response and click on my face to  subscribe to the channel  thank you so much i'll see you soon  you
 

